IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `da-property`
IMPORT `da-vehicles`
IMPORT `da-qa`

-- Duties Act 2008 (WA) -- cases for the Q&A layer (da-qa.l4): every exported question, for every role and every
-- situation.
--
-- Each question is asked for the roles it is not about, with every other input an ASSUMEd value that has none: the
-- answer must be `does not arise for you`, and reading any of those inputs would stop the evaluation with an error ("it
-- is an assumed term"). Each question that takes a situation input is asked, for its own role, with the situation FALSE
-- and every later input ASSUMEd: the answer must be `does not arise for you`. All three situation inputs are BOOLEANs,
-- so no helper reads a situation enumeration through OTHERWISE (graffiti finding 31).
--
-- Every role here is a part of the baseline's seat (the buyer of a home, a car or shares), so each question is asked on
-- the baseline's own facts, with the answer the baseline's case files assert, worked by hand from the text, and checked
-- equal to the baseline export's answer on the same facts.
--
-- Facts from the WA lives: Chloe c051, c074, c081; Daniel d037, d065; Jake k074 (see the baseline's NOTES.md).
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases -- the Q&A layer`

ASSUME `an unasked fact` IS A BOOLEAN
ASSUME `an unasked number` IS A NUMBER
ASSUME `an unasked property` IS A `Kind of property`
ASSUME `an unasked purchase` IS A Purchase
ASSUME `an unasked buyer` IS A Buyer
ASSUME `an unasked company` IS A Company

`as the land buyer` MEANS `I am buying a home or other land in Western Australia`
`as the vehicle buyer` MEANS `I am buying a vehicle, or having its licence granted or transferred to me`
`as the share acquirer` MEANS `I am acquiring shares in a company that may hold land in Western Australia`

